Dragon's breath is like a wand (of fire) and seems to respond to obstacles the same way.  (That is, ricocheting, etc.)  Have you ever zapped a rock (blocking a corridor, say)?  Or a puddle?  Consider walls in a maze as immobile rocks, and I think that should explain the seemingly anomalous behavior of your Dragon's breath.  I would not consider it a bug.


